{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFM1Q7Fw9JqrAgdv4MB7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] A ticket whose reviewer writes `No findings.` merges, and its review log has one round\n[x] A ticket whose reviewer writes an open finding is not merged, its status is `ready-for-human`, its branch still exists, `progress.md` records it as not done, and the run exits 1\n[x] A ticket blocked by an unresolved ticket is reported as blocked and does not run\n[x] A reviewer that exits non-zero or writes unparseable findings fails the attempt, and the ticket goes through the existing retry path\n[x] The reviewer runs with the review role's provider and model, and implementation runs with the implement role's\n[x] The ticket review log round-trips through render and parse, neutralizes sentinel text in free-text fields, and drops malformed entries\n[x] With no `adversarial` key, the agent invocations in a run match today's (no reviewer is spawned for a ticket)\n\nAll seven checklist items are done, but no source code changed. The code for this ticket was already on the branch from earlier commits (US-009 through US-020): the review round runner, the `unresolved` outcome, the per-ticket review log, the fake `pi`, the round label in the display, and the AGENTS.md invariants. Four items already had tests: the review log, the role providers and models, the no-`adversarial` case, and the clean review. I wrote tests for the three that didn't, and they pass against the existing code. So these were written after the code, not failing first.\n\n**Tests added:**\n1. A CLI test in `test/integration.test.ts` where one review decides the outcome (`maxRounds: 1`) and the reviewer returns an open finding. The run exits 1. Ticket 01 becomes `ready-for-human`, its change is not merged, its branch is kept, its worktree is removed, and `progress.md` records it as not done. It is not retried even with `--retries 1`, and ticket 02, which is blocked by 01, never runs but is listed in the output.\n2. Two cases in `test/review-integration.test.ts`, one where the reviewer writes unparseable findings and one where it exits non-zero. Each fails the first attempt, and the retry implements the ticket again and passes. The log records `failed`, then `pass`.\n3. The existing clean-review test now also checks that the ticket's change landed on the base branch, not just that the run finished.\n\n**Verification:** `npm run build`, `npm test` (all suites pass) and `npm run lint` are clean.\n\nI also added a short note to AGENTS.md on how to run a single test. There are two commits, and `.redeye/notes.md` holds the attempt notes, uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":97135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":781},"output_tokens":674,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e10e1272-8092-416a-9383-32ab4ddab6c8","uuid":"5deff55f-3640-4ba6-99f8-efc6481a058c","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:15:09.168Z","request_id":"req_011ChFM1Pw6BMVAnkHbFRxQW"}
